[VOICE]: Off

[STYLE]
Hyperreal industrial sci-fi catastrophe: rusted orbital fortress-cities, weaponized asteroids, glowing fracture cores, dense debris, ruined megastructures, vulnerable planet below. Old, heavy, damaged, dangerous, failing.

[CORE]
Ancient siege weapons disguised as dead asteroids wake from inside. Orange cracks ignite under stone, vent pressure, scrape fortress-cities, fragment, and turn orbit into a collapsing mined belt. Horror = realization, not impact.

[CAMERA]
FPV survival-camera / cockpit-adjacent. Constant survival motion: dodge wreckage, slip through gaps, avoid collisions, shoved by shockwaves. Forward drift, roll, yaw, pitch, debris inches from lens. Tiny ships only as scale needles.

[NEGATIVE]
No cartoon, anime, painterly, glossy CG, clean dogfight, polished ships, laser focus, static shots, slow motion, freeze frames, symmetry, fantasy glow, explosions, hero craft, triumphant ending, calm space.

[SCENES]
0.00–1.00
Impact cut. Camera surges forward as the wide view collapses into threat. A new siege-stone sheds crust, exposing a bright core. Fragments tumble like secondary projectiles.

1.00–2.00
Camera banks left around a broken defense tower. Below, the planet grows larger. Burning objects fall toward atmosphere, but one changes direction: not debris, an active weapon still steering.

2.00–3.20
Knife-pass through dense wreckage. Cables, plates, antenna spines whip inches from lens. Midground bridge folds downward. Background asteroids ignite in sequence, fracture-light pulsing through dust.

3.20–4.20
A colossal weapon-stone drifts overhead, nearly blocking the sky. Underside shows polygonal furnace geometry beneath cracked crust. Incandescent gravel vents like buried engine exhaust.

4.20–5.20
Camera plunges through the vent plume. Visibility collapses into fire haze, ash, rock fragments. Inside the murk, a ruin cluster blows outward from within: another hidden stone waking.

5.20–6.20
Break into a vertical canyon between fortress masses. Falling terraces and spinning plates fill the corridor. Tiny craft dive through. Everything moves downward, outward, failing.

6.20–7.20
Off-frame shockwave shoves camera sideways into partial roll. Plates, dust sheets, scaffolding rip free. Far ahead, a ruin-cluster blooms orange as buried siege-stones activate together.

7.20–8.40
Hard plunge toward the glow. Route tightens between collapsing walls. Right side: half-awakened stone scrapes a fortress face, carving a molten trench and throwing sparks, splinters, torn ribs into orbit.

8.40–9.40
Camera drops under the scrape before structure gives way. A cathedral-scale wall peels outward across frame. Beyond it, more weapon-stones drift in depth: seeded network, not random reaction.

9.40–10.60
Brief scale breath, still moving. Camera clears the wall enough to see the belt across the horizon: ruined spines, stations, drifting plates, igniting stones over the planet. Wreckage interrupts.

10.60–11.60
A burning fragment spins toward lens and misses by inches. Camera snaps downward into lower debris traffic. Flaming wreckage rains planetward. One active stone holds position, then rotates and vents again.

11.60–12.80
Camera threads through a destroyed docking skeleton. Ribs and chambers flash past in heavy parallax. Through gaps, fortress silhouettes erupt internally: siege-stones waking inside architecture like infection.

12.80–13.80
Acceleration surge. Debris streams forward. Tiny ships scatter in panic vectors. A huge awakened stone crosses background while a closer dark one cracks silently, then vents a bright core-flash.

13.80–14.60
Camera bursts from docking skeleton into open space. Not calm: catastrophic read. Orbital graveyard activates across depths, fortress by fortress, stone by stone, over the curved planet.

14.60–15.00
Final hit. A near-frame siege-stone ignites brightest, crust splitting into deployment. Camera yaws to avoid a tumbling megastructure slab.